<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n27103" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">lū^crōsus</span></b> , a,
		um, adj.
		lucrum, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>gainful, profitable, lucrative</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">voluptas,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Ov.
					Am. 1, 10, 35</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Tac.
				Agr. 19</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">fraus lucrosior,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					37, 12, 75, § 197</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">id peraeque etiam lucrosissimum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					18, 31, 74, § 320</span></i>
			.—Hence, adv.: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">lŭcrōsē</span></b> , <i>profitably, advantageously</i>,
					<i><span class="en">Cassiod. Var. 12,
			20</span></i>.—In <i>comp.</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">lucrosius perire,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Hier. Ep. 22</span></i>
			, n. 13 al.</div>
